  "id": "adjustment-method",
  "term": "adjustment method",
  "definition": "In this context, an adjustment method is a statistical way of correcting results when many analysis strategies are tried for the same question, so the chance of false positive findings is reduced. The packet specifically describes the minP adjustment method, which uses the pattern of dependence among tests and a permutation-based estimate of the smallest p-value’s null distribution to control error better than simpler corrections.",
